#: docs/reference/api/io.md:23
msgid ""
"Factory lookup returns an existing face without starting hardware or "
"acquiring a bank. A controller face cannot substitute for an endpoint. A CPU-"
"window lease permits direct loads/stores after acquisition and requires all "
"derived pointer users to join before exact release. Startup backing is a "
"separately selected, reset-time memory plan: its backing ownership already "
"exists before Platform start and lasts while static objects exist. It rejects"
" a whole-bank runtime loan and ordinary Platform stop. Neither profile grants"
" DMA, executable memory, an allocator or physical retention evidence. See the"
" [I/O ownership design](../../design/io-evolution.md) and the selected "
"Board's explicit memory profile."
msgstr ""
"Factory lookup returns an existing face without starting hardware or "
"acquiring a bank. A controller face cannot substitute for an endpoint. A CPU-"
"window lease permits direct loads/stores after acquisition and requires all "
"derived pointer users to join before exact release. Startup backing is a "
"separately selected, reset-time memory plan: its backing ownership already "
"exists before Platform start and lasts while static objects exist. It rejects"
" a whole-bank runtime loan and ordinary Platform stop. Neither profile grants"
" DMA, executable memory, an allocator or physical retention evidence. See the"
" [I/O ownership design](../../design/io-evolution.md) and the selected "
"Board's explicit memory profile."

#: docs/reference/api/io.md:33
msgid ""
"The F407 `sdio-poll` reference requires explicit media activation, uses "
"512-byte sectors, one- or four-bit width and a maximum 12 MHz card clock. CPU"
" polling releases caller buffers on every synchronous return; unresolved "
"card/controller completion still retains the session, pins and gate. Stop "
"succeeds only after complete withdrawal. DMA, IRQ completion, asynchronous "
"cancellation, connected card-detect and hot-swap are not provided by this "
"selected mode."
msgstr ""
"The F407 `sdio-poll` reference requires explicit media activation, uses "
"512-byte sectors, one- or four-bit width and a maximum 12 MHz card clock. CPU"
" polling releases caller buffers on every synchronous return; unresolved "
"card/controller completion still retains the session, pins and gate. Stop "
"succeeds only after complete withdrawal. DMA, IRQ completion, asynchronous "
"cancellation, connected card-detect and hot-swap are not provided by this "
"selected mode."

#: docs/reference/api/io.md:40
msgid ""
"IRQ timestamps and sampled GPIO levels are observations. The F407 EXTI "
"provider marks them COALESCED; that source cannot satisfy the strict NEC "
"source policy. The explicit NEC IRQ-observation reference preserves source "
"flags and publishes sampled/uncertain quality. Protocol inverse checks never "
"establish edge capture completeness or physical timing. See the [infrared "
"source-quality contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/infrared/README.md)."
msgstr ""
"IRQ timestamps and sampled GPIO levels are observations. The F407 EXTI "
"provider marks them COALESCED; that source cannot satisfy the strict NEC "
"source policy. The explicit NEC IRQ-observation reference preserves source "
"flags and publishes sampled/uncertain quality. Protocol inverse checks never "
"establish edge capture completeness or physical timing. See the [infrared "
"source-quality contract](https://github.com/X-Gen-Lab/nexus/blob/NEXUS-"
"DOCUMENTATION-SOURCE/components/infrared/README.md)."

#: docs/reference/api/io.md:47
msgid ""
"For public RS485 composition, use the same exact typed UART reference for "
"`nx_factory_uart_ref()` and `nx_factory_uart_tx_validator_ref()`. The "
"validator getter only returns the existing selected callback; it adds no "
"mutable state or method table and returns NULL for unreviewed modes or IDs. "
"Callback symbols may be shared; pairing with that transport's context and "
"exclusive executor remains a caller precondition. The caller still owns DE, "
"setup/hold timing and joined shutdown. The {ref}`RS485 I/O contract "
"<uart__rs485_8h>` defines that ownership; lookup does not verify transceiver "
"supply, RS485 bus wiring or physical turnaround."
msgstr ""
"For public RS485 composition, use the same exact typed UART reference for "
"`nx_factory_uart_ref()` and `nx_factory_uart_tx_validator_ref()`. The "
"validator getter only returns the existing selected callback; it adds no "
"mutable state or method table and returns NULL for unreviewed modes or IDs. "
"Callback symbols may be shared; pairing with that transport's context and "
"exclusive executor remains a caller precondition. The caller still owns DE, "
"setup/hold timing and joined shutdown. The {ref}`RS485 I/O contract "
"<uart__rs485_8h>` defines that ownership; lookup does not verify transceiver "
"supply, RS485 bus wiring or physical turnaround."

