msgstr "Fill exactly the requested bytes before a finite deadline."

#: docs/reference/api/io.md:195
msgid ""
"Task-only synchronous polling; no heap, worker or OS wait. BUSY causes "
"another clock-bounded poll. The supplied clock must continue advancing "
"throughout the call; changing its domain or stopping its timer violates the "
"contract. NX_DEADLINE_NEVER is rejected. Complete words are emitted least-"
"significant byte first; unused final-word bytes are discarded. A zero-byte "
"request validates face and clock but performs no clock/source access and "
"accepts NULL output. Preflight rejection leaves output unchanged. Once "
"admitted, any error erases the complete output using volatile writes; no "
"partial entropy may be consumed. Output is disjoint from face/table/clock and"
" all their opaque live contexts. This function detects known-span aliases, "
"not opaque extents. Crypto libraries own conditioning, DRBGs and trust "
"policy."
msgstr ""
"Task-only synchronous polling; no heap, worker or OS wait. BUSY causes "
"another clock-bounded poll. The supplied clock must continue advancing "
"throughout the call; changing its domain or stopping its timer violates the "
"contract. NX_DEADLINE_NEVER is rejected. Complete words are emitted least-"
"significant byte first; unused final-word bytes are discarded. A zero-byte "
"request validates face and clock but performs no clock/source access and "
"accepts NULL output. Preflight rejection leaves output unchanged. Once "
"admitted, any error erases the complete output using volatile writes; no "
"partial entropy may be consumed. Output is disjoint from face/table/clock and"
" all their opaque live contexts. This function detects known-span aliases, "
"not opaque extents. Crypto libraries own conditioning, DRBGs and trust "
"policy."

